index b6ee24f..a680d54 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -209,6 +209,12 @@ completed review during the active instance, and those targets form the lineariz
 one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier
 reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
 
+When review results are recorded, the controller appends the review summary to the reviewed patch
+agent's transcript, appends a `work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no` completion prompt, and selects
+that patch-agent session. The prompt is part of the patch-agent chat state so terminal frontends can
+ask for explicit closure after review without losing the reviewed commit bookkeeping used by
+linearization.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
@@ -293,6 +299,12 @@ state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transi
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
 again.
 
+When the selected patch-agent transcript ends with the review-completion prompt, a `yes` or `y` chat
+reply closes that chat locally instead of sending another backend message. Typing follow-up text in
+that chat reopens it and clears the local closed state so additional patch-agent messages can be
+sent. Repeated completion prompts are preserved when they represent later review cycles, so the most
+recent yes/no prompt remains actionable.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
